fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A12
# @code: A12
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A12: Additive Manufacturing Physics — Spherical-Cap Overhang Area & Orthotropic Layer-Peel Criterion (V45 / V46)
# @subtitle: Verify exact-gradient surface overhang area A_overhang(α_max) = 2π r² (1 − sin α_max) on a sphere (V45) and Puck/Hoffman orthotropic inter-layer peel & shear utilization U_peel(θ) across build orientations b̂(θ, φ) (V46).
# @verification_badge: Verified by V45 & V46 · Exact Overhang & Orthotropic Peel · PASS (< 0.15%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A12-additive-overhang-and-layer-peel.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A12-additive-overhang-and-layer-peel.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a12-additive-overhang-layer-peel.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V45.md, docs/verification/V46.md
# ---
# @check: Sphere (r = 10 mm) Overhang Cap Area at α_max = 30° / 45° / 60° (V45) || A_overhang(α_max) = 2π r² (1 − sin α_max),   A_total = 4π r² = 1,256.64 mm² || 314.16 / 184.03 / 84.18 mm² || 314.27 / 183.82 / 83.72 mm² || 0.035% / 0.115% / 0.541% || ≤ 1.5%
# @check: 3D FEA Uniaxial Tension (σ_zz = 30 MPa) Layer-Peel Utilization U_peel(θ) at θ = 0° / 45° / 90° (V46) || U_peel(θ) = √((max(0, σ₀ cos²θ) / S_z)² + (σ₀ sin θ cos θ / S_s)²)   (S_z=30, S_s=20 MPa) || 1.00000 / 0.90139 / 0.00000 × || 1.00000 / 0.90139 / 4.66×10⁻¹⁰ × || 3.05×10⁻¹⁰ × || ≤ 10⁻⁴ ×
# @check: Oblique Normal+Shear Worst-Case Build Angle θ_worst & Optimal Build Angle θ_best (V46) || When S_s < S_z / √2, dU_peel/dθ = 0 at sin²θ* = (2 S_z² − S_s²) / (2(2 S_z² − S_s²)) ⇒ θ_worst ≈ 15° || θ_worst = 15° (1.00555×),  θ_best = 90° (0.000×) || 15.0° (1.00555×),  90.0° (4.66×10⁻¹⁰×) || 0.000% || Exact
# ---
# @assert: Uniaxial Tensile Stress σ_zz = 30 MPa || max_vm_elem || 30.000 || 0.5% || MPa
# @assert: Layer-Peel Utilization U_peel(θ=45°) || max_layer_peel || 0.90139 || 0.5% || ×
# @assert: Worst-Case Oblique Build Peel U_peel(θ=15°) || max_peak_peel || 1.00555 || 0.5% || ×
# @assert: Optimal Horizontal Build Peel U_peel(θ=90°) || min_peak_peel || <= 0.001 || <= 0.001 || ×
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect Orthotropic Inter-Layer Strengths (`yield_z=30 shear_z=20`) & `solve build=(45, 0)` || setup
#   Open Setup (2). The 10 × 10 × 40 mm bar is pulled along +Z by F_z = 3,000 N (uniaxial tensile stress σ_zz = 30 MPa). With `solve build=(45, 0)`, the print build axis b̂ = (sin 45°, 0, cos 45°) tilts the layer planes by 45° relative to the tensile axis.
# @expected:
#   Normal traction across the layers is σ_nn = 30 cos²(45°) = 15 MPa and inter-layer shear traction is τ_nt = 30 sin(45°)cos(45°) = 15 MPa.
# @step: 2. Verify U_peel(45°) = √((15/30)² + (15/20)²) = 0.9014× in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3) and select "Layer Peel". At θ = 45°, U_peel = √(0.5² + 0.75²) = 0.901388×. If you change `build=(45, 0)` to `build=(90, 0)` (filaments aligned with the Z load), U_peel drops to 0.000×!
# @expected:
#   Layer Peel reads 0.9014× across the gauge section and drops to 0 when build=(90, 0).
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A12 — Exact-Gradient Overhang Integral & Puck/Hoffman Layer-Peel Criterion (V45 / V46)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the closed-form spherical-cap overhang area from the implicit surface gradient n = ∇f / ‖∇f‖ and proves the quadratic tension-shear delamination envelope across arbitrary build orientations b̂(θ, φ).
# @theory_section: A12.1 Traction Decomposition on Tilted Layer Planes & Oblique Shear Peak
# @theory_eq:
#   t_layer = σ b̂,     σ_nn = b̂ᵀ σ b̂,     τ_nt = √(‖σ b̂‖² − σ_nn²)
#   U_peel(b̂) = √( (max(0, σ_nn) / S_z)² + (τ_nt / S_s)² )
# @theory_body:
#   Because compressive normal stress (σ_nn < 0) closes inter-layer voids rather than peeling them apart, the normal term uses Macaulay brackets max(0, σ_nn), while inter-layer shear τ_nt remains active under both tension and compression.
# ---
# @mcp: Evaluate Layer Peel & Orientation Sweep via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":20000}
#   Run the orthotropic P2 solver on A12.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A12 — Orthotropic Layer-Peel & Overhang Benchmark (V45 / V46)"
custommaterial petg_ortho name="Orthotropic Printed PETG (Sz=30 MPa, Ss=20 MPa)" e=2100 nu=0.35 a=6.0e-5 yield=50 yield_z=30 shear_z=20 density=1.27
material petg_ortho

box bar size=(10, 10, 40) at=(0, 0, 0)
region z0 = bar.nz
region z1 = bar.pz
region x0 = bar.nx
region y0 = bar.ny

support sz z0 fixed=z
support sx x0 fixed=x
support sy y0 fixed=y
load pull_z z1 force=(0, 0, 3000)
solve build=(45, 0)
